          "item": {
            "@type": "NewsArticle",
            "headline": "BigEndian Semiconductors Raises $6M Led by IAN Alpha Fund to Commercialise Its First System-on-Chip",
            "articleSection": "Discovery & Research",
            "abstract": "Indian semiconductor startup BigEndian Semiconductors has secured $6 million in funding led by IAN Alpha Fund, with the capital earmarked to commercialise its first system-on-chip product, expand its product engineering team, and deepen partnerships with foundries, IP ecosystems, and OEMs. The raise is notable in the context of India's push to build a domestic semiconductor industry, as BigEndian represents a rare homegrown chip design company reaching commercial readiness. The investment also reflects growing domestic venture confidence in India's semiconductor ambitions following recent government fab approvals.",
            "url": "https://yourstory.com/2026/05/bigendian-semiconductors-bags-6-million-led-by-ian-alpha-fund",
            "publisher": {
              "@type": "NewsMediaOrganization",
